# `presets/` — read-only map presets for the editor

Drop `.SC2Bank` save files here to use them as **presets** in the Cute Defense
map editor (`tools/cutedefense-map-editor.html`). Presets load read-only — the
editor never writes back to this folder, so a preset can never be saved over.

## Naming convention

```
<Mode> - <Map Name>.SC2Bank
```

`<Mode>` must be one of the editor's mode labels (case-insensitive); `<Map Name>`
is free text. The first ` - ` separates the two. Examples:

```
Standard - Crossroads.SC2Bank
Duos Versus - Twin Lanes.SC2Bank
Tug of War - Big Push.SC2Bank
Tower Defense - Spiral.SC2Bank
```

Valid `<Mode>` labels: `Standard`, `Versus`, `Duos Versus`, `Quick`, `Attrition`,
`Horde`, `Maze Wars`, `Tower Defense`, `Tug of War`.

Files that don't match this pattern (e.g. the editor's own
`CustomCuteDefenseMap<Mode><Slot>.SC2Bank` exports) are ignored by the preset
picker.

## How to use

1. In the editor sidebar, under **Presets**, click **Choose presets folder…**
   and pick this folder.
2. Pick a map from the **Preset** dropdown and click **Load preset (read-only)**.
   The editor switches to the preset's mode and loads its layout.
3. To save your own edits, use **Save .SC2Bank** as usual — it downloads a fresh
   `CustomCuteDefenseMap<Mode><Slot>.SC2Bank`, leaving the preset untouched.

The editor is an offline `file://` page, so it can't watch the folder; you pick
it once per session (the browser doesn't persist `file://` folder access).

These `.SC2Bank` files are not gitignored — commit any presets you want to share.
